Z||000000||Formula88||04-08-2001||05:31 PM||||Ok, people.  I've searched, but haven't found any good comparisons.  Anyone out there with a 3800SC, V8 or even 3.4TDC care to share some performance stories.  I'd love to hear any races between V8's and 3800SCs.  I'm trying to consider options for a future F355 kit car project.  It's gotta be fast (duh), but why put in a SBC if a 3800SC is faster?  N* would be great, but probably too expensive.  I like the idea of the 3.4TDC, but I want more power than that, and the high maintenance requirements of this engine make me a bit wary.  Anyone care to post some performance numbers?||||reg||10
Z||000001||Phil||04-08-2001||05:46 PM||||SC3800's can give you low to mid 13 sec 1/4 mile so go from there. With no mods.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">   <BR>SC 3800<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 04-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||gabriel||04-09-2001||03:08 PM||||&gt;I'm trying to consider options for a future F355 kit car project.<P>  I've considered the 3800SC option for my 355 project (I've also got the TR project mostly finished)  but I just can't bring myself to drop an auto into a Ferrari clone.<BR>(And IMHO, the Ferrari kits are a cast iron B**ch to do) - But they do look great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  If you can deal with the issues of mating a 3800SC with a manual, then you still will deal with the issues of shelling the tranny.<P>  But I do think that swaping a 3800 turbo<BR>(ala cwest) with a manual 5 speed might be one sweet option.  I'm swapping out a modified 3800SC/465E into a fiero now, but I don't have the dyno #s yet.<P>  Also the exhaust would be very expensive to improve - I'm about to fabricate my own headers & that is the current hangup here.<P>  If you start this project, be sure to let us know how things are going ...||||reg||1
Z||000003||IndySid||04-09-2001||10:44 PM||||I own an '84 Indy with a 300hp/350 V8.  It's modified but let me tell you, the torque is incredible!  It's a matter of personal preference which engine you decide to go with.  Both options have their advantages and disadvantages.  Good luck, Sid ||||reg||14
